Z||000000||Gold87SE||09-25-2000||11:34 PM||||A while ago I asked about what would be best way to get them to stay on and everyone told me RTV. Now it's time to put them on. Where can I get RTV?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold87SE||09-25-2000||11:46 PM||||I'm talking about the Pontiac logos.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||09-26-2000||12:48 AM||||RTV Blue,=general purpose<BR>Ultra Blue,=High performance, oily surfaces<BR>RTV Red,=High temp<P>All are silicone adhesives/sealants. <BR>You can get it at any auto parts store.<P><BR>DXR_DAD<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000003||deceler8||09-26-2000||10:09 AM||||You can also use any kind of window caulk if you have a tube around...anything that says "silicone" or "siliconized" will be more than adequate.<P>GE also makes a general purpose clear silicone adhesive that you can get just about anywhere and this will work too. In fact, this stuff is so versatile you'll find all kinds of uses for it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||09-26-2000||10:16 AM||||Stuff called Automotive GOOP probably would work good too.  Goes on clear, dries clear.  May also find it called as Household GOOP.<P>I use it to glue the peeling back edge of the soles of my shoes back on.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">         <BR>         <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000005||wilburt||09-26-2000||10:48 AM||||HugGRRRFiero, I'm wondering if we think the same way....Two months ago I happily spent $546.00 on tires for my '87 GT. Last week I needed some new work boots, went down to K-mart for the 'Blue light special'. $36.00??!!?!! No way! Bought a tube of GOOP and now I've got at least 6 more months on this pair!!! Shows where my priorities are!  ||||reg||14
